# CLAUDE.md — agent guardrails for this repo

## Change size
- Keep PRs small and single-purpose. If a change touches more than ~200 lines
  or more than 3 modules, split it, unless it's mechanical (rename, formatting).

## Spec discipline
- The architecture spec lives at `docs/architecture.md` and uses numbered,
  anchored sections (see agent-workflow-orchestrator/docs/spec-convention.md).
- Never rewrite the whole spec file. Only the agent loop patches named sections.

## Tests
- Never delete a test or weaken an assertion to make CI pass.
- If a change makes an existing test's expectation wrong, add a new test
  documenting the new expected behavior and leave a comment flagging the
  conflict for human review — don't resolve it yourself.
- New behavior needs a new test in the same PR, not a follow-up.

## Commit / PR format
- PR description must state: intent, risk tier (trivial/moderate/needs-deep-review),
  and your own confidence + reasoning in one sentence.
- Commit messages: imperative mood, one logical change per commit.

